From: switch-v8 horizon port
Subject: [PATCH] Redirect MemoryChunk flag writes on CODE pages through the rw alias (W^X)

On Horizon, executable memory is a libnx jit_* CodeMemory region with two
aliases of the same physical pages: rx (execute, NOT writable) and rw (writable
= rx + horizon_jit_rw_delta). V8 addresses everything via the rx alias and patch
0003 redirects instruction-stream writes (WritableJitAllocation) to the rw
alias.

But the GC marking barrier also writes the *MemoryChunk header flags* that live
at the start of every page: MutablePage::SetOldGenerationPageFlags ->
RawSetTrustedAndUntrustedFlags -> `Chunk()->untrusted_main_thread_flags_ = ...`.
For a CODE-space page that header is on the rx (read-only) alias, so the write
faults: Data Abort @ 0x0 in SetOldGenerationPageFlags <- Activate/DeactivateSpaces
(marking-barrier.cc), with the fault address inside the code arena. This only
happens under full JIT (no code arena exists when jitless). Confirmed on device:
full JIT crashed after 32 MiB while jitless reached 3110 MiB in the same regime.

V8 already has a W^X-aware variant for single flags (SetFlagMaybeExecutable wraps
the write in RwxMemoryWriteScope when is_executable()), but SetOldGenerationPageFlags
uses the non-executable raw path. Rather than reroute all callers, fix it at the
single write site: in RawSetTrustedAndUntrustedFlags, when the chunk is a code
page, write untrusted_main_thread_flags_ through the rw alias (rx + delta). For
non-code pages horizon_jit_rw_delta() returns 0, so this is a no-op.

This mirrors the V8_HORIZON_JIT_WRITE redirect from patch 0003, applied to the
in-page chunk-flags store.
---
 src/heap/mutable-page-inl.h | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/heap/mutable-page-inl.h b/src/heap/mutable-page-inl.h
index d5e99637..479b4549 100644
--- a/src/heap/mutable-page-inl.h
+++ b/src/heap/mutable-page-inl.h
@@ -10,6 +10,14 @@
 
 #include "src/heap/base-page-inl.h"
 
+#if V8_OS_HORIZON
+// Horizon W^X: the MemoryChunk header of a CODE page is on the read-only rx
+// alias; its flag writes must go through the writable rw alias = rx + delta.
+// horizon_jit_rw_delta() returns 0 for non-code addresses (no-op). See patch
+// 0003 (V8_HORIZON_JIT_WRITE) and mman-horizon.cc.
+extern "C" intptr_t horizon_jit_rw_delta(uintptr_t rx_addr);
+#endif
+
 namespace v8::internal {
 
 // static
@@ -80,7 +88,21 @@ V8_INLINE void MutablePage::RawSetTrustedAndUntrustedFlags(
   SBXCHECK_EQ(untrusted_main_thread_flags, trusted_main_thread_flags_);
 #endif  // V8_ENABLE_SANDBOX
   trusted_main_thread_flags_ = new_flags;
+#if V8_OS_HORIZON
+  // Write the in-page flags through the rw alias. For a CODE page Chunk() is on
+  // the read-only rx alias; rx + horizon_jit_rw_delta() is the writable alias.
+  // For non-code pages the delta is 0, so this is a plain store. The two code
+  // aliases map the same physical pages and are D-cache coherent, so the GC's
+  // later reads via the rx alias observe this write (no I-cache sync needed;
+  // these are data flags, not instructions).
+  MemoryChunk* chunk = Chunk();
+  auto* flags_ptr = reinterpret_cast<MemoryChunk::MainThreadFlags*>(
+      reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(&chunk->untrusted_main_thread_flags_) +
+      horizon_jit_rw_delta(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(chunk)));
+  *flags_ptr = trusted_main_thread_flags_;
+#else
   Chunk()->untrusted_main_thread_flags_ = trusted_main_thread_flags_;
+#endif
 }
 
 void MutablePage::SetFlagsUnlocked(MemoryChunk::MainThreadFlags flags,
